7/19/26, 12:03 PM SOP-SYS-002 - Corrupted System File Repair

# STANDARD OPERATING PROCEDURE

## Resolution of OS Corruption using DISM and SFC

| Document ID    | SOP-SYS-002                     | Version        | 1.0       |
| :------------- | :------------------------------ | :------------- | :-------- |
| Department     | IT Service Desk / L1 Tech Support | Effective Date | July 2026 |

## 1. Objective

To repair operating system files, resolve application hangs, patch random Blue Screen of Death (BSOD) errors, and restore core Windows stability.

## 2. Scope

Applicable to all Windows 10 and Windows 11 desktop environments showing signs of OS corruption or performance degradation.

## 3. Pre-requisites & Warnings

*   Requires an active internet connection so the DISM tool can fetch clean replacement files from Windows Update.
*   The scan process may take 15–30 minutes to complete.

## 4. Step-by-Step Procedure

### 4.1 Launch Elevated Command Prompt

file:///C:/Users/ADMIN/Downloads/gemini-code-1784442621280.html 1/3
```

```markdown
7/19/26, 12:03 PM SOP-SYS-002 - Corrupted System File Repair

*   Search for **cmd** in the Windows start menu, right-click, and choose **Run as administrator**.

### 4.2 Scan and Repair the Windows Component Store Health

*   Check the local image repository integrity:

    ```
    DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /ScanHealth
    ```

*   If errors or component corruption are reported, execute the recovery command:

    ```
    DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth
    ```

### 4.3 Execute System File Checker (SFC) Scan

*   Once the servicing image is verified clean, scan the active operating system files:

    ```
    sfc /scannow
    ```

*   Wait for the verification phase to hit 100%.

### 4.4 Interpret SFC Terminal Outputs

*   **No Integrity Violations:** System structure is healthy.
*   **Successfully Repaired:** System files were broken but fixed. (Issue resolved).
*   **Unable to Fix:** Corrupt assets remain. (Requires Escalation).

### 4.5 Perform System Reboot

*   Safely restart the workstation to finalize repairs:

    ```
    shutdown /r /t 0
    ```

## 5. Expected Outcome
---
Corrupted Windows system binaries are automatically replaced with healthy, authenticated versions, stabilizing the environment.

